# <n>Rust<> SpeedSheet Tips
Tips for using the <doc rust>Rust SpeedSheet<> Like a Pro

<block light><image "rust-overview-light.webp"><><block not-light><image "rust-overview-dark.webp"><>

#### Master Search / Find

<b>Find<> is your best friend. Here’s why:

<*>Finds it fast
Shows only what you want
1-2 words returns results
Incomplete names match too<>


#### Use the '-only' Shortcut

Use '-only' or just '-' with the item name to focus on its section alone and drop the indirect uses from your results:

<*>"<c><doc "rust?vec-only>vec-only<><>"
"<c><doc "rust?vec->vec-<><>"<>


#### Lookup by Path

Find a type by entering either it's full path or just the "::":

<*>"<c><doc "rust?std::vec::vec>std::vec::vec<><>"
"<c><doc "rust?::vec>::vec<><>"<>


#### Lookup Symbols

Need to know what a symbol does? Just enter "symbol" and then the symbol you what:

<*>"<c><doc "rust?symbol ::\<>symbol ::\<><><>"<><>


#### Use ESC to Reset

When you’re done searching, hit Escape to clear your search and bring everything back into view.

<*>ESC clears your search<>


#### Top Sections to Explore

Don’t miss these key areas:

<*><doc "rust?hello world>Hello World<>
<doc "rust?smart pointer guide>Smart Pointer Guide<>
<doc "rust?struct-only>Structs<>, <doc "rust?trait-only>Traits<><>


